# .dockerignore: what never enters the Docker build context (spec 25 §3.2 rule 5).
# Why: keeps the image small and, above all, keeps private material out of it:
#   .work/ and brief/ must never reach the build context (confidentiality rule).
# What: excludes VCS and CI files, private notes, azd state, env files, local
#   dependencies and builds, tests, evaluation, docs, specs and infra.
# Must not: exclude backend/app, backend/pyproject.toml, backend/uv.lock, config/
#   or frontend/ sources (the Dockerfile needs them). AC-25.6.
.git
.github
.work
brief
.azure
.env*
**/.env*
**/node_modules
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/.cache
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/*.tsbuildinfo
frontend/dist
backend/tests
backend/scripts
eval
docs
specs
infra
.claude
